# Line endings are load-bearing in this tree.
#
#   * os/scripts/* is run by bash. A CRLF checkout leaves a CR at the end of
#     every line, so `set -euo pipefail` becomes `set -euo pipefail<CR>` and
#     bash rejects `pipefail` as an option name; five unrelated tests fail.
#   * contract/openapi.json is SHA-256 pinned by contract/openapi.sha256, so a
#     CRLF checkout changes the bytes and the provenance test fails.
#   * the systemd units, mkosi config and the JSON/YAML manifests are parsed on
#     a Linux image, where a trailing CR becomes part of the parsed value.
#
# A Windows clone with the default `core.autocrlf=true` hit all three. Pin LF
# in the repository and on checkout, on every platform, so the bytes here are
# the bytes a Linux runner or the appliance image sees.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the files where a stray CR is a real defect rather than a
# cosmetic one, so narrowing `*` later cannot quietly reintroduce it.
*.sh text eol=lf
os/scripts/* text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
